# {{ project-name }}

Runnable Axum service generated from Rust Web Foundry.

The default service is intentionally small: production composition, MySQL readiness, configuration, observability, graceful shutdown, and quality gates are enabled without installing example business routes or schema. A richer canonical Task slice is available behind the default-off `reference-task` feature. It is executable architectural and DDD reference material, not a universal task-management domain model.

## Prerequisites

- Rustup
- Docker with Compose v2
- curl
- cargo-generate `>=0.23.14, <0.24.0`
- Just `>=1.58.0, <2.0.0`
- sqlx-cli `>=0.9.0, <0.10.0`

```sh
rustup update stable
cargo install cargo-generate --version 0.23.14 --locked
cargo install just --version 1.58.0 --locked
cargo install sqlx-cli --version 0.9.0 --locked --no-default-features --features rustls,mysql
```

## Verify the generated service

```sh
just verify
```

`just verify` proves both configurations: the default server has health/readiness but no Task API, while the opt-in reference configuration exercises Task HTTP, Domain/Application behavior, MySQL persistence, TaskPolicy integration, trace propagation, and shutdown behavior.

For direct default operation, copy `.env.example` to `.env`, then run:

```sh
cargo run -p {{ project-name }} -- migrate
cargo run -p {{ project-name }} -- serve
```

To run the reference Task service instead:

```sh
just policy-stub
just migrate-reference-task
just serve-reference-task
```

The server never runs migrations automatically.

## Architecture

```text
http ────────────┐
                 ├──> application ───> domain
infrastructure ──┘

app ──> http + infrastructure + application + domain
```

Requested behavior and explicitly confirmed decisions own intended business/public semantics. Source, tests, manifests, migrations, and quality commands own current executable facts. If they conflict, surface the conflict instead of silently treating the reference Task domain as a source of user requirements.

Feature work starts from the nearest complete production path and its tests. Use the Task reference only when its implementation pattern answers a concrete design question. See [architecture](docs/guide/architecture/README.md), [Domain modeling](docs/guide/domain/modeling.md), the [Task flow](docs/guide/task-flow.md), and [development](docs/guide/development.md).

## Rust review

The project pins `leonardomso/rust-skills` for fresh, review-only use and applies project-specific overrides for Clean Architecture and the selected stack:

```sh
bash scripts/install-rust-skills.sh
```

Then explicitly invoke `.agents/skills/review-rust-web/SKILL.md` in a fresh review session with the request and complete diff. The generated project may add its own Skills or local agent instructions later; template-default minimalism is not an application architecture rule.

## Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `just infra-up` / `just infra-down` | Start or stop local MySQL |
| `just migrate` | Run the default migration boundary; no reference schema is installed |
| `just serve` | Start the default production server without Task routes |
| `just policy-stub` | Run the opt-in TaskPolicy reference peer |
| `just migrate-reference-task` | Apply reference Task migrations |
| `just serve-reference-task` | Start the server with the `reference-task` slice |
| `just sqlx-prepare` | Refresh SQLx metadata against the reference schema |
| `just test` | Run default and reference workspace tests against existing MySQL |
| `just architecture` | Check objective workspace dependencies and the small project/review contract |
| `just check` | Check both feature shapes, format, Clippy, DB-free tests, SQLx style, and project contract |
| `just ci` | Run checks, default/reference acceptance, SQLx verification, and lifecycle proof against existing MySQL |
| `just verify` | Start MySQL and run the complete CI proof locally |
